  "english": "BOOK OF CANONS\nOF THE RESURRECTION OF OUR LORD JESUS CHRIST\nEASTER SUNDAY. IN THE NIGHT\nNo vigil. And they shall place the Holy Sacrament [relics/vessels] upon the cushion-stand in the chancel.\nCanon-head, Tone 1 [ahz]: \"Judge, O Lord, those...\" [Psalm 34 [35]:1].\nAnd the priests shall vest together and come into the chancel, and begin the Hymn of the Day, Tone 1 [ahz]: \"Today He rose.\" Canticle, Tone 8 [deg]: \"Today great good news,\" with its accompanying verses.\nThe Myrrh-bearing Gospel, John, the last portion: 20:1, \"And on the first day of the week,\" to verse 18, \"she said to him.\"\nDuring this fifty-day period of Pentecost on Sundays, the Myrrh-bearing Gospel: read the last portion of the three chapters, and that of Matthew, read the same. But when they say the last verse of the \"Praise the Lord from the heavens,\" everyone shall kiss one another, saying: \"Christ is risen from the dead. Great tidings [good news] to you and to us!\"\nSong: \"The Resurrection.\" Litany: \"Let us all say.\" \"Holy God, who rose from the dead.\" Until the Ascension, the Song and the \"Holy God\" are these.\n\nAnd the priests shall vest together and go out in procession with the Cross and the Gospel, with incense and candles and all adornment, singing the hymn, Tone 1 [ahz]: \"Today He rose.\" Psalm 64 [65]: \"To you is due praise.\" Acts 1:1, \"The first book,\" to verse 8, \"of the earth.\" Alleluia: \"They were standing.\" Gospel, Mark 16:2, \"And early in the morning,\" to verse 8, \"for they were afraid.\"\n\nAnd then they shall sing the hymn, and read the four Gospels facing the four corners of the world. First: hymn, Tone 1 [ahz]: \"With the dawning,\" facing the East. Stand [Orthi]. Gospel, John 19:38, \"After this,\" to verse 42, \"they laid Jesus.\" Facing the West, singing the hymn, Tone 2 [ak]: \"You were sent from the Father.\" Gospel, Luke 23:50, \"And behold, a man,\" to verse 56, \"according to the commandment.\" Facing the South, singing the hymn, Tone 3 [bzh]: \"At Your grave.\" Gospel, Mark 15:42, \"And when evening came,\" to Mark 16:1, \"they might come and anoint Him.\" And facing the North, singing the hymn, Tone 4 [bk]: \"To Your resurrection.\" Gospel, Matthew 27:57, \"And when evening came,\" to verse 66, \"along with the guard.\"\n\nAnd then they shall enter the chancel, singing the hymn, Tone 1 [ahz]: \"Who Your immaculate arms.\" Then, Psalm 4: \"There was signed,\" alternating with \"In my calling.\" Gospel, John 19:16, \"Then he delivered Him,\" to verse 22, \"what I have written, I have written.\" Litany: \"For the peace from above.\" And they shall bless the fields [Antasdan]. Litany: \"By this Holy Cross.\" Prayer: \"Protect [us].\"\n\nAnd then they shall begin the Introit: \"For He is risen.\" Hymn, Tone 8 [dk]: \"The Only-begotten Jesus,\" for the Mother of God, for the Cross, and \"Glory.\" Psalm 129 [130]: \"Let Your ears be attentive,\" alternating with \"Out of the depths have I cried.\" Gospel, John 11:1, \"Now there was a certain sick man,\" to verse 46, \"what Jesus had done.\" Then they shall say the \"For the Souls\" [memorial prayers], and after that: Song, \"Newly-created,\" say it fully. Litany...",
